<title>USA: US 10-yr indexed note sale high yield 3.449 pct.</title>
<headline>US 10-yr indexed note sale high yield 3.449 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Treasury said its Dutch bidding auction of inflation-indexed 10-year notes produced these results:</p>
<p>			 10-YEAR NOTES DUE JAN 15, 2007</p>
<p>			     $7.003 BILLION AUCTION</p>
<p>	     YIELD			  PRICE	COUPON</p>
<p> HIGH	3.449    Awarded At	99.482	3.375</p>
<p> MEDIAN    3.400    High Yield	NOT GIVEN  Percent</p>
<p> LOW	 3.200    75 Percent	NOT GIVEN</p>
<p>	   Cover - (Bids Over Amount Sold)    =  5.31 Times</p>
<p> U.S. TREASURY (GOVERNMENT DEBT)		 MATURITY 15.Jan.07</p>
<p> MATURITY/TYPE    10-YEAR NOTES		  PAY DATE 06.Feb.97</p>
<p>							   LAUNCHED 29.Jan.97</p>
<p> ISSUED/ACCEPTED   7.003 BLN USD		 CUSIP   9128272M3</p>
<p> BIDS SUBMITTED   37.219			   COUNTRY	  USA</p>
<p> NONCOMPETITIVE   157.00 MLN			  DUTCH AUCTION</p>
<p> NY FED DISTRICT    N.A.			   COUPON	 3.375</p>
<p> FOREIGN INSTITN  0.00 MLN			 PRICE	 99.482</p>
<p> BIDDING RANGE    3.200-3.449 PCT		YIELD-HIGH   3.449</p>
</text>
